WiFi module: CEL CMP9611 (NXP IW611 chipset, identifies internally as SDIW612)
Interface: SDIO on uSDHC2 (GPIO2_IO13-18), WiFi reset GPIO4_IO21 (SAI2_RXFS), PDn# GPIO1_IO00
Power: USB OTG only (no separate VIN), 3.3V to module pins 49/50
Boot: jumper on module pin 52 (BOOT_MODE0), low=eMMC, high=USB SDP
eMMC: uSDHC3 (internal to module, not on carrier pins)
Build host: Ubuntu 24.04 desktop in VirtualBox on Windows 11

Yocto build: Ka-Ro BSP scarthgap branch

Machine: qsxp-ml81, Distro: karo-minimal
Kernel: linux-karo 6.6.52 (NOT linux-imx — important for .bbappend naming)
U-Boot: u-boot-karo 2025.07

Key fixes required (all confirmed working):

Ka-Ro layer.conf — removes nxpiw612-sdio from MACHINE_FEATURES by default; delete that line from meta-karo-nxp/conf/layer.conf’s MACHINE_FEATURES:remove block
local.conf additions:
MACHINE_FEATURES:append = " nxpiw612-sdio nxpwifi-all-sdio"
DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " wifi"
UBOOT_CONFIG = "default noenv mfg"
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " dropbear"
U-Boot variant — karo-minimal distro only builds noenv and mfg variants by default; must add default to UBOOT_CONFIG — the noenv variant ignores saveenv entirely, causing cold boot failure. Flash u-boot-qsxp-ml81-default.bin to mmc0boot0
Kernel recipe name — Ka-Ro uses linux-karo, not linux-imx; .bbappend must be named linux-karo_%.bbappend
Kernel config fragment — linux-karo uses kernel.bbclass + cml1.bbclass (not kernel-yocto.bbclass), so .cfg files in SRC_URI are NOT auto-merged. Must use do_configure:append() to cat the fragment manually
NXP driver Android defaults — nxp-wlan-sdk Makefile defaults to CONFIG_ANDROID_KERNEL=y which disables cfg80211; fix via .bbappend:
EXTRA_OEMAKE += "CONFIG_ANDROID_KERNEL=n CONFIG_STA_CFG80211=y CONFIG_UAP_CFG80211=y"

Both nxp-wlan-sdk_%.bbappend AND kernel-module-nxp-wlan_%.bbappend need this

CONFIG_CFG80211 — not enabled in Ka-Ro’s default kernel config; causes “struct has no member ‘wdev’” errors without the fragment fix above
Devicetree — imx8mp-cmp9611-wifi.dtsi added via #include in imx8mp-qsxp-ml81.dts; staged via do_configure:append + install into ${S}/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/ since Ka-Ro’s overlay staging mechanism doesn’t auto-copy non-registered files
U-Boot environment — bootcmd_mmc in default compiled environment missing loadfdt; fix once at first boot:
setenv bootcmd_mmc run loadfdt loadkernel bootargs_mmc
setenv append_bootargs root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 rw
saveenv

